In article <1990Mar15.172240.878@cec1.wustl.edu> Scott Edward Conrad writes:
>I got an error message:
>
>	Suddenly, the dungeon collapses
>	Error: makemon?  more-|
>
>	Is there a time limit or a random number generator which will
>cause the dungeon to collapse (or does my Nethack have a mind of its own)

No.  The nethack developers simply violated the first rule of error
handling: "Give an error message that the user will understand."  They
chose to give a "cute" error message instead.  If you look in your
save directory you should find a file whose name ends in ".e" or
".e.Z" (if it is compressed).  The ".e" stands for error.  Usually
these errors are recoverable (yay team!) so you can copy the file to
one without the ".e" in the name (be careful about overwriting newer
savefiles).  Then play and the file will be restored.

